      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes #55087. GLM-5.3 KDA merges the q/k/v short-conv weights into one cached tensor (`_merged_conv_weight`), built lazily on first forward. Online-RL workflows warm up with dummy weights (cache built), then refit `q_conv1d`/`k_conv1d`/`v_conv1d` — but the cached merge is never invalidated, so inference silently keeps using the pre-refit convolution weights.\n\n## Approach\n\nWeight loading dispatches on the param's stamped `weight_loader` (`getattr(param, \"weight_loader\", default_weight_loader)` in `AutoWeightsLoader`). So the cache can be invalidated at exactly the point the weights change: in `Glm5NextLinearAttention.__init__`, wrap each conv weight's stamped loader so any write clears `_merged_conv_weight`. The next forward rebuilds it from the current params. No new hooks, no changes to the reload machinery.\n\n## Coverage / limitations\n\n- ✅ Initial load (loaders run before first forward; cache built after anyway)\n- ✅ Checkpoint-format refit: `reload_weights` → `model.load_weights` → stamped loaders → cache cleared\n- ✅ Layerwise reload: re-dispatches through the same stamped loaders\n- ❌ Kernel-format refit (`param.copy_` bypass) writes params without loaders — the cache is NOT invalidated there. That path also skips every other derived-weight rebuild in the tree (same class of limitation); noted for follow-up if it matters in practice.\n\nA `_version`-based approach was considered and rejected: the default loader writes via `param.data.copy_`, which bumps neither `param._version` nor `param.data._version` (verified on torch 2.10/ROCm), so version tracking cannot see the main refit path.\n\n## Verification\n\nAd-hoc functional test on MI350X against a real `Glm5NextLinearAttention` (gloo TP1, minimal `Glm5NextConfig`):\n\n| Step | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Build layer, populate merge cache | OK |\n| Refit `q_conv1d` through its real stamped weight loader | cache **invalidated** |\n| Next merge uses refit values | OK |\n| No refit → cache persists (no spurious invalidation) | OK |\n\nPre-commit: all hooks pass. No GPU-unit test added (KDA layer requires a full `VllmConfig` + mamba cache plumbing; happy to add one if maintainers want it).\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
